sec.p:
The dimensions and mass of each specimen were measured before and after sintering to determine the shrinkage and mass loss. For each experimental condition, three specimens were measured, and the results were reported as mean
±
standard deviation (SD;
n = 3
). The same specimens were subsequently subjected to compressive strength testing using an electronic universal testing machine (WH-5000) at a loading rate of 1 mm/min. The force–displacement data recorded during testing were converted into stress–strain curves, from which the compressive strength of each specimen was determined. The compressive strength data were likewise reported as mean
±
SD (
n = 3
).
